IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `more-maintenance`

-- Maintenance Orders (Reciprocal Enforcement) Act 1975, ss 2-10, 14(3), 16, 17(2) -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case or subsidiary legislation (none was retrieved).
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_maintenance-orders-reciprocal-enforcement-act-1975.py). Expected results were written by
-- hand from the text.

§ `s 2`

#ASSERT `is a maintenance order under the Act` `monthly maintenance by a man to his wife`
#ASSERT `is a maintenance order under the Act` `a lump sum by a man to his former wife`
#ASSERT NOT `is a maintenance order under the Act` `monthly maintenance by a woman to her husband`
#ASSERT `is a maintenance order under the Act` `monthly maintenance by a father to his child`
#ASSERT `is a maintenance order under the Act` `monthly maintenance by a mother to her child`
#ASSERT `is a maintenance order under the Act` `birth expenses payable by an adjudged father`
#ASSERT `is a maintenance order under the Act` `funeral expenses of a child payable by an adjudged father`
#ASSERT NOT `is a maintenance order under the Act` `a bare finding of paternity`
#ASSERT NOT `is a maintenance order under the Act` `maintenance of a parent by an adult child`

§ `ss 3, 17(2)`

#ASSERT `the payee may apply to send the order abroad` `monthly maintenance by a man to his wife` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the payee may apply to send the order abroad` `monthly maintenance by a woman to her husband` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the payee may apply to send the order abroad` `monthly maintenance by a father to his child` TRUE TRUE FALSE

